1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,000
Nov 4, 13:00 UTC.

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:07,800
43,500 swaps in one day. 95% came back refunded.

3
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:19,000
A 1Click swap: quote, deposit, intent on NEAR, solver fill.

4
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:30,000
When no solver fills it, the funds go back: a refund.

5
00:00:31,700 --> 00:00:37,700
Intents Desk counts every swap, every hour.

6
00:00:37,700 --> 00:00:43,700
One partner's swaps: 100% bad for 24 hours.

7
00:00:43,700 --> 00:00:52,700
Rule: 50+ swaps and 50% bad in an hour opens an incident.

8
00:00:53,600 --> 00:00:57,300
Paste a deposit address or any tx hash.

9
00:00:57,300 --> 00:01:02,300
One answer first: what happened to your funds.

10
00:01:02,300 --> 00:01:12,300
The timeline and every tx, with its NEAR block.

11
00:01:12,300 --> 00:01:18,100
Copy a support message. No addresses in it.

12
00:01:19,300 --> 00:01:25,300
Case → intent hash → NEAR block → explorer.

13
00:01:25,300 --> 00:01:31,800
Anyone can check it on chain.

14
00:01:32,500 --> 00:01:38,200
Incidents get a report for the teams who can fix them.

15
00:01:38,200 --> 00:01:45,200
Who should look, block range, commands to reproduce.

16
00:01:45,200 --> 00:01:49,000
Download the evidence as CSV or JSON.

17
00:01:49,700 --> 00:01:57,000
Intents Desk: data for NEAR Intents support.

